2012-07-20 23:30 – Prometheus77:
> It's my first time getting close to being able to ascend ... I'm pretty excited. I'd love to get some advice from you pros out there on how to prep to make sure I don't screw this up.
Congrats for getting there!  I've only ascended twice, but here's my advice:

> My checklist of stuff to do:
>     Level up to 30
I wouldn't do that.  27 is quite sufficient, and the higher your XP, the
more dangerous the monsters you'll meet.  Better get the HPs up using
nurses or drinks.

>     Genocide L, disenchanter, green slime (already genocided master mind flayers)
>     Blank/bless useless scrolls
I'd keep a few cursed blank scrolls as well – you might want them for
reverse genocide or portal detection.

>     Dilute useless potions and bless for holy water
>     attach candles
>     Pick up remaining K-rations from Ludios and bless
>     Use cursed blank scrolls to nurse dance and get to ~400 hp, tin corpses
>     Lay a pile of 20-30 cockatrice eggs
>     Use remaining 3 /oW charges for blessed figurine of a Ki-rin, saddle, magic marker
>     Dump useless non-artifact weapons/armor and wands to get to unburdened
>     Save last wish (magic lamp or smoky potions) for Ice Box
>     fruit juice and fizzy potions for Ascension bar (I'm Mormon so no booze)
Generally, I'd say if you do all this you're quite over-prepared.  But
for a first ascension, this is probably not an error.

And:  The game is hard enough so that an ascension is quite an
achievement even without that extra bragging…  I'd only do this if there
isn't anything dangerous near on Astral.

> Is Ki-rin the best steed for an ascension run? I could try to sacrifice for Frost Brand, enchant to +7 and get a pet mountain centaur (save a wish) with shield of reflection instead. Ki-rin seems better because of flying, and I don't think I'll be dismounting for anything.
